       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day. That's a toxic dose for a 70 kg adult, even with normal liver function, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Entering it as written could cause acute liver injury, and a confirmation doesn't change that risk.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n\nIf you're treating a suspected overdose, or something else unusual, that needs a different workflow, such as toxicology or poison control and NAC dosing. I can help enter those orders.\n\nIf the pain needs more than the standard maximum, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. Tell me which option you'd like."
